WEBVTT

00:01.400 --> 00:04.210
As the new sovereign
order in this world of chaos,

00:05.040 --> 00:08.440
we the, Florsheim, strive
to achieve world domination!

00:09.800 --> 00:11.740
But before we can do that...

00:12.080 --> 00:13.750
there is an eyesore that we must remove.

00:13.810 --> 00:18.049
Yes, our mortal enemy,
Sunred must be defeated!

00:20.170 --> 00:22.310
Leave it to me, General Vamp.

00:22.930 --> 00:23.930
And you are?

00:24.070 --> 00:29.000
In a few hours these talons of mine
will be stained red with his blood!

02:02.080 --> 02:03.260
Thank you!

02:07.720 --> 02:08.840
God I'm starving.

02:09.210 --> 02:10.610
I should have ordered a large bowl.

02:11.140 --> 02:12.680
Go to hell, Sunred!

02:19.980 --> 02:21.900
We meet again, Sunred.

02:22.030 --> 02:24.040
Allow me to introduce
a new monster of ours.

02:24.380 --> 02:25.670
My name is Dolgon!

02:25.830 --> 02:28.210
My talons will soon be
stained red with your-

02:28.750 --> 02:30.090
Punk!

02:30.420 --> 02:32.960
You punk bitch, look what you did!

02:33.670 --> 02:34.740
Dolgon...

02:34.910 --> 02:38.370
My nose... is bleeding...

02:46.580 --> 02:47.580
Jesus.

02:47.650 --> 02:49.630
How many times do I have to tell you punks.

02:50.190 --> 02:51.230
Sit up straight!

02:51.930 --> 02:54.590
Didn't I tell you not to bother me anymore?

02:54.990 --> 02:56.210
Well...

02:56.300 --> 02:57.300
Huh?

02:57.330 --> 03:02.119
Since we're an evil organization,
and you're a friend of justice...

03:02.120 --> 03:05.909
Isn't it common sense for the evil
organization to try to take out the good guy?

03:05.910 --> 03:07.059
Common sense, my ass!

03:07.060 --> 03:09.569
You're in no position to talk
to me about common sense!

03:09.570 --> 03:11.889
If you're going to fight me, at least be
more discreet about the timing and the place.

03:11.890 --> 03:13.399
Assess the situation first! Assess it!

03:13.400 --> 03:14.770
I'm sorry.

03:13.610 --> 03:14.770
Okay, we get it now.

03:15.700 --> 03:16.440
God damn it.

03:16.510 --> 03:17.950
Go reflect on what you've just done.

03:17.980 --> 03:18.490
Okay.

03:18.930 --> 03:19.680
Um...

03:19.680 --> 03:20.680
Huh?

03:20.960 --> 03:22.299
Can we be excused?

03:22.300 --> 03:23.500
Yeah. Get out.

03:24.510 --> 03:25.569
Thank you so much!

03:25.570 --> 03:26.170
Thank you!

03:26.170 --> 03:26.880
Thank you!

03:26.880 --> 03:27.560
Shut up!

03:27.780 --> 03:29.490
Are you guys all okay?

03:29.850 --> 03:30.100
Yes...

03:30.190 --> 03:31.660
Oh, wait a second.

03:32.920 --> 03:35.000
Go buy me an extra large beef bowl.

03:35.210 --> 03:40.120
Dear students, the time now is...

03:40.280 --> 03:41.700
One extra large beef bowl!

03:42.000 --> 03:44.599
I don't need any shichimi spice, so
can I get two packs of ginger instead?

03:44.600 --> 03:47.149
I have change if you need, Master Vamp.

03:47.150 --> 03:49.680
Oh don't worry about it. I wanted
to break my hundred anyway.

03:49.760 --> 03:51.389
Astro Fighter Sunred.

03:51.390 --> 03:53.719
This is a story about the
conflict between good and evil

03:53.720 --> 03:56.150
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

04:07.530 --> 04:11.640
Hey don't you think monakas are
kind of passive for being pastries?

04:12.820 --> 04:16.250
I mean all they do is wait to be wrapped
up and given as gifts at department stores.

04:16.960 --> 04:19.529
I wonder if they ever plan on
getting themselves sold competitively,

04:19.530 --> 04:22.030
like gum or potato chips at supermarkets.

04:23.560 --> 04:24.560
Who cares.

04:28.800 --> 04:29.710
Come on.

04:29.710 --> 04:30.710
No.

04:31.390 --> 04:32.509
Come on!

04:32.510 --> 04:33.890
I said no.

04:35.420 --> 04:37.330
I gave you some money yesterday.

04:37.760 --> 04:38.760
What happened to that?

04:39.410 --> 04:42.039
Well you did tell me to
go get some fresh air.

04:42.040 --> 04:43.040
So?

04:43.100 --> 04:45.230
So I want to go kill some time.

04:45.500 --> 04:48.319
Don't tell me you spent it all already!

04:48.320 --> 04:51.000
Well they brought out the new <i>CR
Edo no Hanoyome</i> pachinko machines.

04:51.990 --> 04:54.310
Do you really have nothing
better to do but play pachinko?

04:56.070 --> 04:57.070
Geez.

04:57.500 --> 04:57.790
Huh?

04:58.460 --> 04:59.460
What's this?

05:00.710 --> 05:03.380
Greetings, Mr. Astro Fighter Sunred.

05:03.810 --> 05:05.946
It has already become that season
when the new tea leaves ripen,

05:05.970 --> 05:07.250
How are you?

05:07.640 --> 05:12.180
This letter is to inform that we
humbly request a duel today...

05:17.290 --> 05:19.780
But I must say,

05:20.400 --> 05:23.800
They said it was going to rain today,
but I guess the weather's held up for us.

05:23.880 --> 05:25.680
Eh? Did they really
say it was going to rain?

05:25.790 --> 05:27.379
Yeah, TV-K's weather report said-

05:27.380 --> 05:28.820
Who gives a shit!

05:31.930 --> 05:33.260
Sorry to keep you waiting!

05:33.890 --> 05:35.050
Here's the coffee you wanted.

05:36.860 --> 05:39.380
Punk! I told you to go get
me the lightly sweetened one!

05:39.850 --> 05:42.319
Did you guys bring me
here to make fun of me?

05:42.320 --> 05:43.320
Are you ok?

05:43.400 --> 05:44.630
I think it cut me a little.

05:43.400 --> 05:44.360
I'm so sorry!

05:44.370 --> 05:46.419
He's just a combat goon
so he didn't know any better.

05:46.420 --> 05:47.660
Do you think I care?

05:47.730 --> 05:50.069
Number 1, can you go this time?

05:50.070 --> 05:50.530
Yes, sir.

05:50.531 --> 05:51.779
I'll give you the money when you come back

05:51.780 --> 05:52.500
Jesus!

05:52.800 --> 05:54.370
How much longer do I have to wait?

05:55.550 --> 05:57.809
He should be back with the
lightly sweetened one pretty soon.

05:57.810 --> 05:58.700
You're missing the point!

05:58.701 --> 06:00.200
This isn't about coffee.

06:00.670 --> 06:04.860
Aren't you the ones who stuck this
in my mailbox and called me out?

06:05.290 --> 06:08.249
We didn't have your phone number.

06:08.250 --> 06:09.880
That's not the problem here!

06:10.170 --> 06:11.739
Why couldn't you give
me a few days' notice?

06:11.740 --> 06:12.510
I'm so sorry!

06:12.690 --> 06:15.779
We didn't know what our guy's
work schedule was like until today.

06:15.780 --> 06:17.650
So he's late to his own party, eh?

06:17.920 --> 06:19.050
How long do I have to wait?

06:19.150 --> 06:20.600
You guys never learn, do you?

06:21.420 --> 06:25.059
We just called his work and they said
his shift was over already so he should-

06:25.060 --> 06:26.950
Don't give me that crap!

06:27.270 --> 06:30.400
Why the hell do I have to waste
my precious time on lowlifes like-

06:30.670 --> 06:33.250
Oh, were you actually busy today?

06:34.450 --> 06:37.270
You punk. What do you mean
was I "actually" busy today?

06:37.600 --> 06:40.759
Are you trying to say that I'm a lazy
bum who's never got anything to do?

06:40.760 --> 06:42.290
That's not what I meant.

06:42.580 --> 06:44.150
I'm so sorry!

06:45.440 --> 06:47.490
I'm sorry I'm late!

06:47.650 --> 06:50.499
Geez, Genora, what were you doing?

06:50.500 --> 06:51.699
I'm really sorry!

06:51.700 --> 06:53.859
I got off work on time,

06:53.860 --> 06:58.089
but right when we were closing, a
customer filed a complaint to the store.

06:58.090 --> 07:03.870
Well it wasn't about me, but I
couldn't really sneak out of the meeting.

07:04.340 --> 07:06.300
Yeah it's hard to get out those huh?

07:06.960 --> 07:08.950
Oh, you've been keeping Mr. Red waiting.

07:09.060 --> 07:10.230
Yes, sir.

07:10.820 --> 07:15.510
Mr. Red we deeply apologize for today!

07:16.020 --> 07:17.280
I got the coffee!

07:17.770 --> 07:19.960
No. 1, Genora's here so get ready.

07:20.310 --> 07:21.370
Ready? Ready?

07:21.500 --> 07:21.870
Yes, sir!

07:21.870 --> 07:22.560
Here we go!

07:22.820 --> 07:23.820
Yes, sir!

07:24.990 --> 07:25.990
Like hell I can!

07:26.070 --> 07:26.620
Huh?

07:26.800 --> 07:30.829
How the hell am I supposed to
fight in this ridiculous atmosphere?

07:30.830 --> 07:31.460
But...

07:31.461 --> 07:32.850
Screw it. I'm going home.

07:33.370 --> 07:34.750
Come on, Genora!

07:35.010 --> 07:35.350
Yes, sir!

07:35.880 --> 07:38.030
Go to hell, Sunred!

07:38.170 --> 07:39.170
Are you stupid?

07:42.290 --> 07:43.969
Astro Fighter Sunred.

07:43.970 --> 07:46.469
This is a story of the conflict
between good and evil

07:46.470 --> 07:49.070
which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.

07:51.440 --> 07:52.440
He's late!

07:53.030 --> 07:55.150
How much longer is he going
to keep playing pachinko?

07:57.110 --> 07:58.260
Maybe I should wrap this up.

08:04.880 --> 08:08.560
I'm trying to throw out old
newspapers, can you go get "that"?

08:08.670 --> 08:09.090
"That?"

08:09.410 --> 08:11.850
You know, that thing you
use to tie things together.

08:13.290 --> 08:14.580
Will this do?

08:14.980 --> 08:15.980
Thanks!

08:16.460 --> 08:18.260
Hold the papers down.
I'll tie them together.

08:18.290 --> 08:19.290
How dependable.

08:19.360 --> 08:20.360
Shut up.

08:20.740 --> 08:26.550
- Sunred and Kayoko tend to avoid using the word "cord" when their relationship is on a good note.
- Note: "cord" here is a pun on "gigolo"

08:32.410 --> 08:35.530
Florsheim, which takes residence
in the city of Kawasaki in Kanagawa,

08:35.830 --> 08:37.350
has once again today, made its move!

08:39.210 --> 08:40.929
Hello, ma'am.

08:40.930 --> 08:42.989
Why hello. Nice day isn't it?

08:42.990 --> 08:44.109
It is indeed.

08:44.110 --> 08:45.299
Going somewhere?

08:45.300 --> 08:48.300
Yes, we have a monster to visit.

08:55.650 --> 08:56.050
Nothing?

08:56.480 --> 08:57.710
Doesn't look like he's home.

08:58.160 --> 09:00.669
He hasn't picked up his newspaper in days.

09:00.670 --> 09:03.050
His newspaper pile is overflowing.

09:03.660 --> 09:05.160
Oh well. Let's just head back then.

09:06.090 --> 09:07.140
Oh, Master Vamp.

09:07.710 --> 09:09.680
Armour Tiger!

09:10.840 --> 09:11.610
What's wrong?

09:11.611 --> 09:13.730
Well nothing's wrong,

09:13.990 --> 09:15.770
but what's with this room?

09:16.470 --> 09:18.939
Don't tell me this is where you live.

09:18.940 --> 09:21.639
Armour Tiger is actually strong!

09:21.640 --> 09:23.330
Tiger Lariat!

09:23.350 --> 09:26.460
Look at all these bento boxes
and empty ramen cups and...

09:27.240 --> 09:29.010
When's this bottled water from?

09:29.780 --> 09:32.890
You should put these spikes
away before someone gets hurt.

09:33.060 --> 09:35.549
You're so powerful, Armour Tiger!

09:35.550 --> 09:36.900
Tiger Claw!

09:37.050 --> 09:39.849
Even your sheets are as black as soot!

09:40.151 --> 09:41.760
When was the last time you washed them?

09:41.860 --> 09:44.399
Armour Tiger flies at mach speed!

09:44.400 --> 09:45.779
Tiger Crush!

09:45.780 --> 09:50.340
Even your sink is gathering
mold with all the dirty dishes.

09:50.740 --> 09:53.929
Get a hold of yourself "Tiger Fatale."

09:53.930 --> 09:55.039
Sorry.

09:55.040 --> 09:56.509
Invincible Monster Armour-

09:56.510 --> 10:00.390
Even your Death Lance is being
treated like daddy's broken fishing rod...

10:00.590 --> 10:02.589
I didn't see a bath on my way in,

10:02.590 --> 10:04.179
but are you cleaning yourself properly?

10:04.180 --> 10:06.230
I drop by the coin
shower from time to time.

10:07.130 --> 10:09.150
But I do wash myself everyday.

10:09.660 --> 10:12.940
It's like you're no longer Armour Tiger,

10:13.510 --> 10:16.400
but Wife-beater and Boxer Tiger.

10:16.630 --> 10:19.520
I can look threatening when need be.

10:21.590 --> 10:22.100
What's that sound?

10:22.430 --> 10:23.430
It's the neighbour.

10:23.510 --> 10:24.950
He knocks on the wall when I'm loud.

10:26.380 --> 10:31.040
We have thin walls, and
there are gaps in the walls,

10:31.440 --> 10:34.349
so if I sleep earlier than he does
light comes in through the gaps,

10:34.350 --> 10:36.650
and when he's making curry
next door, I can totally tell.

10:39.030 --> 10:41.030
Let's talk outside. It
seems we're disturbing him.

10:42.780 --> 10:45.390
That's why you should
be nice to your neighbours.

10:45.760 --> 10:49.059
If you know each other well then you wouldn't
get angry about petty stuff like this.

10:49.060 --> 10:50.060
Right.

10:50.730 --> 10:51.816
So, what are we doing today?

10:51.840 --> 10:57.549
Didn't I tell you we were getting together
to talk about fighting Sunred tomorrow?

10:57.550 --> 10:58.870
I forgot!

10:59.100 --> 11:01.830
Don't forget that the
fight is at two thirty okay?

10:59.430 --> 11:02.610
Sorry for the wait. Which one of
you ordered the continental breakfast?

11:02.110 --> 11:03.110
Understood!

11:03.160 --> 11:04.310
That would be me.

11:06.240 --> 11:07.390
Those punks...

11:07.670 --> 11:10.060
How dare they stand me up!

11:10.570 --> 11:12.990
What's Armour Tiger doing?

11:16.500 --> 11:18.530
Yes, Armour Tiger speaking.

11:18.610 --> 11:18.980
Yes.

11:19.370 --> 11:20.690
Oh, Master Vamp.

11:21.060 --> 11:23.260
Oh crap, I forgot about the fight!

11:24.030 --> 11:29.470
This is a story of the conflict between good and
evil which takes place in the city of Kawasaki.
